// Title: Dumping Process via Sqldumper.exe
// Sigma ID: 23ceaf5c-b6f1-4a32-8559-f2ff734be516
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Kirill Kiryanov, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-08 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.001
// Description: Detects process dump via legitimate sqldumper.exe binary
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate MSSQL Server actions
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/countuponsec/status/910977826853068800
//   - https://twitter.com/countuponsec/status/910969424215232518
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Sqldumper/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_susp_sqldumper_activity.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\sqldumper.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "0x0110" or ProcessCommandLine contains "0x01100:40")
